  VALUES (v_test, v_sec, $q$I'd rather you ------- smoke in the house.$q$, 'multiple_choice', 1, $q$'Would rather' + person + past simple.$q$, 6) RETURNING id INTO v_q;
  VALUES (v_test, v_sec, $q$The teacher made us ------- the exercise again.$q$, 'multiple_choice', 1, $q$'Make' + object + bare infinitive.$q$, 7) RETURNING id INTO v_q;
  VALUES (v_test, $q$reading1$q$, $q$Reading — Part 1$q$, $q$reading$q$, NULL, NULL, $q$A Day at the Market

Every Saturday, the old market in our town fills with colour and noise. Stalls selling fruit, flowers and second-hand books line the narrow streets, and the smell of fresh bread drifts from a small bakery at the corner. I have been going there since I was a child, when my grandfather used to take me to buy cheese from a man called Mr Garcia.

Last month, I discovered that the market might close. The council wants to turn the square into a car park, saying that fewer people shop at market stalls these days. Many of the traders are worried, since some of them have worked there for more than thirty years. A group of local people has started a petition, and I signed it immediately.

I don't think a car park would solve anything. People come to the market not just to buy things but to meet friends and talk. Supermarkets can offer low prices, but they cannot offer that feeling of community.$q$, NULL, 1)
  RETURNING id INTO v_sec;
  VALUES (v_test, v_sec, $q$What does the writer say about the market on Saturdays?$q$, 'multiple_choice', 1, $q$'The old market… fills with colour and noise.'$q$, 0) RETURNING id INTO v_q;
  VALUES (v_test, v_sec, $q$Why does the council want to close the market?$q$, 'multiple_choice', 1, $q$The council wants a car park, saying fewer people shop at market stalls.$q$, 1) RETURNING id INTO v_q;
  VALUES (v_test, v_sec, $q$What did the writer do about the plan?$q$, 'multiple_choice', 1, $q$'I signed it immediately.'$q$, 2) RETURNING id INTO v_q;
  VALUES (v_test, v_sec, $q$What does the writer think people come to the market for?$q$, 'multiple_choice', 1, $q$People come 'not just to buy things but to meet friends and talk'.$q$, 3) RETURNING id INTO v_q;
  VALUES (v_test, $q$listening1$q$, $q$Listening — Part 1$q$, $q$listening$q$, NULL, $q$لا يتضمن هذا القسم ملفًا صوتيًا بعد — اقرأ نص التسجيل كما لو كنت تسمعه (مرة واحدة فقط في الامتحان الحقيقي)، ثم أجب عن الأسئلة.$q$, $q$Monologue: a woman talks about her first job

"I got my first job when I was sixteen, working in a bookshop at weekends. I wasn't paid much, but I loved it, because I could read during quiet moments. The owner, Mr Evans, was very strict about punctuality, and I once lost half an hour's pay for being five minutes late. At the time I thought that was unfair, but I learned a lot from it. The busiest day was always Saturday, when tourists came in looking for guidebooks. I stayed there for two years, until I left for university. Looking back, I think that job taught me more about dealing with people than any course I took later."$q$, NULL, 2)
  RETURNING id INTO v_sec;
  VALUES (v_test, v_sec, $q$How old was the speaker when she got the job?$q$, 'multiple_choice', 1, $q$'When I was sixteen.'$q$, 0) RETURNING id INTO v_q;
  VALUES (v_test, v_sec, $q$What did she like most about the job?$q$, 'multiple_choice', 1, $q$She loved it because she could read during quiet moments.$q$, 1) RETURNING id INTO v_q;
  VALUES (v_test, v_sec, $q$Why did she lose half an hour's pay?$q$, 'multiple_choice', 1, $q$She was five minutes late.$q$, 2) RETURNING id INTO v_q;
  VALUES (v_test, v_sec, $q$What does she say she learned from the job?$q$, 'multiple_choice', 1, $q$The job taught her about dealing with people.$q$, 3) RETURNING id INTO v_q;
  VALUES (v_test, $q$Writing — Part 1: Essay (ungraded practice)$q$, 40, $q$اكتب مقالًا من 140–190 كلمة. قارن مع النموذج بعد الانتهاء.$q$, $q$WRITING PART 1 — Essay (140–190 words)

In your English class you have been talking about technology. Now your teacher has asked you to write an essay.

Write an essay using ALL the points below:

"Mobile phones have made our lives better."
Do you agree?

Write about:
1. communication
2. education
3. (your own idea)

Write your essay in 140–190 words.$q$, $q$Mobile phones are now a part of everyday life, and in my opinion they have mostly made our lives better, although they also bring some problems.

First of all, phones have revolutionised communication. We can talk to friends and family anywhere in the world, send photos in seconds and call for help in an emergency. For people who live far from their relatives, this is extremely valuable.

Secondly, phones can support education. Students can look up information, use dictionary apps and watch lessons online. A learner of English, for example, can practise vocabulary on the bus. However, phones can also distract students in class, so they must be used sensibly.

Another important point is safety and convenience: maps, banking and transport apps save us a lot of time. On the other hand, many people spend too many hours on social media, which can affect sleep and concentration.

To sum up, mobile phones offer great benefits for communication, learning and everyday life, provided that we control how much we use them.$q$);
END $ep$;

-- English Level Placement Test (A1–C1)
