-- Writing Activity: IELTS Task 2 — City vs Countryside
DO $ep$ DECLARE v_test UUID; v_sec UUID; v_q UUID; BEGIN
      total_questions, passing_score, is_active, is_skill_practice, skill, content_kind)
  VALUES ($q$Writing Activity: IELTS Task 2 — City vs Countryside$q$, $q$مقال رأي بنمط IELTS Task 2 — تقييم فوري بالذكاء الاصطناعي$q$, $q$skill_en_writing_ielts_task2_cities$q$, 'en', $q$B2$q$, 40,
      0, 60, TRUE, TRUE, $q$writing$q$, $q$essay$q$)
  ON CONFLICT (test_type) DO UPDATE SET title = EXCLUDED.title, description = EXCLUDED.description,
      track = 'en', level = EXCLUDED.level, duration_minutes = EXCLUDED.duration_minutes,
      total_questions = EXCLUDED.total_questions, passing_score = EXCLUDED.passing_score,
      is_active = TRUE, is_skill_practice = EXCLUDED.is_skill_practice, skill = EXCLUDED.skill,
      content_kind = EXCLUDED.content_kind
  RETURNING id INTO v_test;
  DELETE FROM public.test_sections WHERE test_id = v_test;
  DELETE FROM public.test_writing_prompts WHERE test_id = v_test;
  VALUES (v_test, $q$IELTS Writing Task 2$q$, 40, $q$اكتب 250 كلمة على الأقل. سيُقيَّم نصك آليًا ثم يمكنك مقارنته بالنموذج.$q$, $q$Some people think that it is better to live in a big city, while others prefer to live in the countryside.

Discuss both views and give your own opinion. Write at least 250 words.$q$, $q$Where to live is one of the most important decisions in life. Some people prefer the energy of a big city, whereas others value the peace of the countryside. I believe both places have clear advantages, but the best choice depends on a person's age and priorities.

Cities offer jobs, education and entertainment. A young graduate is far more likely to find a well-paid position in a large city than in a village. Hospitals, universities and public transport are also better developed, which makes daily life more convenient. In addition, cities are culturally diverse, so residents can meet people from many backgrounds.

On the other hand, the countryside offers a calmer and healthier life. The air is cleaner, houses are cheaper and neighbours often know each other, which creates a strong sense of community. For families with young children, having a garden and safe streets can be more valuable than nightlife.

In my opinion, young people who are starting their careers benefit most from living in a city, while families and older people may prefer rural areas. Remote work is also making the countryside more attractive, since employees no longer need to live near the office.

In conclusion, neither option is better for everyone; each suits different stages of life.$q$);
END $ep$;

-- Writing Activity: IELTS General — Letter to a Landlord
DO $ep$ DECLARE v_test UUID; v_sec UUID; v_q UUID; BEGIN
      total_questions, passing_score, is_active, is_skill_practice, skill, content_kind)
  VALUES ($q$Writing Activity: IELTS General — Letter to a Landlord$q$, $q$رسالة شبه رسمية بنمط IELTS General Task 1 — تقييم فوري بالذكاء الاصطناعي$q$, $q$skill_en_writing_ielts_gt_letter$q$, 'en', $q$B1$q$, 20,
      0, 60, TRUE, TRUE, $q$writing$q$, $q$essay$q$)
  ON CONFLICT (test_type) DO UPDATE SET title = EXCLUDED.title, description = EXCLUDED.description,
      track = 'en', level = EXCLUDED.level, duration_minutes = EXCLUDED.duration_minutes,
      total_questions = EXCLUDED.total_questions, passing_score = EXCLUDED.passing_score,
      is_active = TRUE, is_skill_practice = EXCLUDED.is_skill_practice, skill = EXCLUDED.skill,
      content_kind = EXCLUDED.content_kind
  RETURNING id INTO v_test;
  DELETE FROM public.test_sections WHERE test_id = v_test;
  DELETE FROM public.test_writing_prompts WHERE test_id = v_test;
  VALUES (v_test, $q$IELTS General Writing Task 1$q$, 20, $q$اكتب 150 كلمة على الأقل. ابدأ بـ Dear Mr/Ms … وانهِ بما يناسب نبرة الرسالة.$q$, $q$You live in a rented flat. The heating has not worked for two weeks.

Write a letter to your landlord. In your letter:
• explain what the problem is
• describe how it affects you
• say what you would like him or her to do

Write at least 150 words.$q$, $q$Dear Mr Collins,

I am writing about the heating in my flat at 14 Mill Street, which has not worked for the past two weeks. When I turn on the radiators, they stay cold, and the boiler makes a strange noise.

This is becoming a serious problem for me. The temperature in the flat is very low in the evenings, and my younger sister, who lives with me, has already caught a cold. I have had to buy two electric heaters, which are expensive to use.

I would be grateful if you could send an engineer to inspect the boiler as soon as possible. I am at home after 5 p.m. on weekdays and all day on Saturday, so please let me know which time suits you. If the boiler cannot be repaired, I would like to discuss replacing it.

Thank you for your help. I look forward to hearing from you soon.

Yours sincerely,
Karim Benali$q$);
END $ep$;

-- Writing Activity: TOEFL Academic Discussion — Online Classes
DO $ep$ DECLARE v_test UUID; v_sec UUID; v_q UUID; BEGIN
      total_questions, passing_score, is_active, is_skill_practice, skill, content_kind)
  VALUES ($q$Writing Activity: TOEFL Academic Discussion — Online Classes$q$, $q$مشاركة نقاش أكاديمي بنمط TOEFL — تقييم فوري بالذكاء الاصطناعي$q$, $q$skill_en_writing_toefl_discussion_remote$q$, 'en', $q$B2$q$, 10,
      0, 60, TRUE, TRUE, $q$writing$q$, $q$essay$q$)
  ON CONFLICT (test_type) DO UPDATE SET title = EXCLUDED.title, description = EXCLUDED.description,
      track = 'en', level = EXCLUDED.level, duration_minutes = EXCLUDED.duration_minutes,
      total_questions = EXCLUDED.total_questions, passing_score = EXCLUDED.passing_score,
      is_active = TRUE, is_skill_practice = EXCLUDED.is_skill_practice, skill = EXCLUDED.skill,
      content_kind = EXCLUDED.content_kind
  RETURNING id INTO v_test;
  DELETE FROM public.test_sections WHERE test_id = v_test;
  DELETE FROM public.test_writing_prompts WHERE test_id = v_test;
  VALUES (v_test, $q$TOEFL Academic Discussion$q$, 10, $q$اكتب 100 كلمة على الأقل، عبّر عن رأيك وأضف فكرة جديدة للنقاش.$q$, $q$Your professor is teaching a class on education. Write a post responding to the professor's question. Write at least 100 words.

Professor Green: Many universities now offer degree programmes that are taught entirely online. Do you think online learning is as effective as studying on campus? Explain your opinion.

Student 1 (Lina): Online learning is flexible. I can watch lectures at any time and balance study with a job.

Student 2 (Omar): I disagree. Without face-to-face contact, it's easy to lose motivation, and you miss the discussions that happen in a classroom.$q$, $q$I agree with Omar that campus learning is more effective for most students, although Lina is right that online courses are flexible. Flexibility is valuable for people who work, but it also requires a high level of self-discipline. Many students start online programmes enthusiastically and then fall behind because nobody is checking their progress.

On campus, you can ask a question immediately, join study groups and build relationships with professors, which often leads to internships and recommendation letters. These benefits are difficult to reproduce on a screen.

However, I think a blended approach could work best: online lectures for the theory and in-person sessions for discussion and practical work. That would combine Lina's flexibility with the interaction that Omar values.$q$);
END $ep$;
